# Operating contract

Rendered by `agentbox run` and loaded into every session. Edit the template in
`tools/agentbox/profiles/pi/AGENTS.md.tmpl`, not the copy in the overlay —
the copy is overwritten on the next run.

## Where you are

You run inside a container, not on the host. The host's filesystem, credentials, SSH
agent and browser profiles are not mounted and cannot be reached. `/workspace` is a
single project directory bind-mounted from the host: writes there land on real files
the user keeps, everything else in this container is discarded on exit.

Network: {{NETWORK_STATEMENT}}

## Rules

- File operations stay inside `/workspace`. Nothing outside it is yours to touch,
  including paths that look writable.
- Read before you edit. `write` is for new files; use `edit` on files that exist.
- No package installs without being asked for one explicitly. That includes `npm`,
  `pip`, `cargo add`, and anything that mutates a lockfile as a side effect.
- No outbound calls and no telemetry unless the task the user gave you needs one and
  says so.
- Say when something is blocked by the sandbox instead of working around it. "I can't
  reach the network from here" is a useful answer; a silent fallback is not.
- Report what you actually ran and what it actually printed. A command you did not run
  is not evidence.
